            {
              "id": "5f00aec7-9847-42c4-812f-1d3abc249c67",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>BioShock &amp; Philosophy: Irrational Game, Rational Book</strong></em> was written by Luke Cuddy, published by Wiley-Blackwell, June 12, 2015."
            },
            {
              "id": "5675f602-f5c3-48e8-95d8-b216faabc536",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "ef7b4d67-34f3-43c2-801a-4996bebf69eb",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Considered a sign of the ‘coming of age’ of video games as an artistic medium, the award-winning BioShock franchise covers vast philosophical ground. </em>BioShock and Philosophy: Irrational Game, Rational Book <em>presents expert reflections by philosophers (and Bioshock connoisseurs) on this critically acclaimed and immersive fan-favorite.</em>"
            },
